[Objective]:

This challenge will create a file named `delete_me` in the home directory. You must delete this file and then run /challenge/check for the flag.

[Key Concept]:

The `rm` command deletes files, the argument provided is the file you want deleted. For example `rm example` would remove the `example` file.

[Solution]:

Simply invoke `rm delete_me` in the home directory, then run `/challenge/check` for the flag.

[# Relevant command(s) or code]:

The `rm` command removes files, the argument passed to the command is the file you're requesting to delete.

